    "q-4310": {
      "dom_id": "step-q4310",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251141/assets/fc485a3c47295e08c917d1c9a2e90df0a0d6eaa931f4df23e17700da1536ca6e.png)\n\nIn the quadrilateral $OMNP$ shown above, find the measure of $∠N.$",
      "worked_solution": "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding up the internal angles and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠M+m∠N+m∠P+m∠O & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {104}^{∘}+(10x-{4}^{∘})+{104}^{∘}+{76}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 10x+{280}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 10x & ={80}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={8}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠N & =10x-{4}^{∘} \\\\  & =10({8}^{∘})-{4}^{∘} \\\\  & ={76}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
